   "n": 32,
   "kind": "h2",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Strategy Summary"
  },
  {
   "n": 33,
   "kind": "summary",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Core Philosophy & Mechanics"
  },
  {
   "n": 34,
   "kind": "h4",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Core Thesis"
  },
  {
   "n": 35,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "The VIX is a mean-reverting fear gauge. When markets price in maximum fear, they historically precede the strongest recoveries. This strategy mechanically increases leverage exposure when fear is highest and reduces it during complacency."
  },
  {
   "n": 36,
   "kind": "h4",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "The Four ETFs"
  },
  {
   "n": 37,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "BIL — SPDR Bloomberg 1–3 Month T-Bill ETF. Near-cash stability. Preserves capital in calm markets; reduced as crisis opportunity grows."
  },
  {
   "n": 38,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "SPY — SPDR S&P 500 ETF. Broad market exposure. The steady core position across all tiers."
  },
  {
   "n": 39,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "QQQ — Invesco Nasdaq-100 ETF. Growth and tech concentration. Increases meaningfully as VIX rises."
  },
  {
   "n": 40,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "TQQQ — ProShares UltraPro QQQ 3× Leveraged ETF. Maximum recovery capture at peak fear. Highest risk, highest reward potential. Never exceeds 25% of the portfolio.",
   "flags": [
    "disclaimer or risk wording"
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 41,
   "kind": "h4",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Rebalancing Rules"
  },
  {
   "n": 42,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Rebalance monthly on the first trading day of each month. Additionally, rebalance immediately when the VIX crosses into a different tier — either up or down."
  },
  {
   "n": 43,
   "kind": "h4",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Time Horizon"
  },
  {
   "n": 44,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Minimum 10 years. TQQQ's volatility decay requires extended compounding to overcome. This strategy is inappropriate for any capital needed within 5 years."
  },
  {
   "n": 45,
   "kind": "h4",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "Risk Acknowledgment",
   "flags": [
    "disclaimer or risk wording"
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 46,
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "region": "main",
   "text": "This is not financial advice. For educational and informational purposes only. Past performance is not indicative of future results. TQQQ can lose 70–95% of its value in severe bear markets. Never invest more than you can afford to lose completely.",
   "flags": [
    "disclaimer or risk wording"
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 47,
   "kind": "paragraph",
